📗
  📔 An app's description of itself as an OpenAPI 3.1 document: every route
  that is not hidden, with what its pattern, its notes, its shapes and the
  answers it said it gives tell of it. It is written once, the first time the
  app is asked anything, which is after every route was registered, and kept.

  What a route is asked by whom is read as the guard reads it: the note that
  the guard was told, and whether it is closed where a route says nothing. An
  app without a guard has no route that asks for a token, whatever its notes
  say.

  OpenAPI tells the parameters of a path apart by where they stand, and not
  by their names or by what they are: /kinds/{id} and /kinds/{name} are one
  path to it. So routes that differ only in that are one path here too,
  under the names of the route that was registered first, and each declares
  its own parameters under those names. Of two such routes with one method
  the document can hold one. It holds the first, and the other is left out
  and said so.
